22 entries now. The new ones:

**D18 — no re-fold after interrupt.** You were right to re-raise this: I measured it earlier, reported it in chat, and never wrote it to the doc. It's in now. `canFoldSettled = settled && !interrupted && !error && foldableCount >= 2` — an interrupted turn emits no `TurnFold` row at all, so the control is gone regardless of your choice. D10 makes it hit every time.

**D20 — blank regions on scroll.** Found a contradiction. `message-timeline.tsx:748` sets `overscan: 50`, but the custom `rangeExtractor` directly below it replaces that with `renderOverscan()` — which is **1** on a cold mount and **6** after measurements exist. So the real band is 1–6 rows and the `overscan: 50` literal is dead. A fast flick outruns six rows of tall transcript turns, which is your blank area filling in as you arrive.

Worth flagging: `timeline-virtualization.ts:118` documents this *exact* symptom as already fixed ("a fast flick scrolls skipped rows into the viewport before the browser renders them, showing estimate-sized blank boxes" — they removed `content-visibility: auto` for it). You're seeing it again, so either that regressed or six rows was never enough. That same comment claims "the overscan band is small (≤6 rows)" while `overscan: 50` sits a few lines away — one of the two is wrong on its face.

**D21 — no scrollbar in expanded tool calls.** Confirmed, and deliberate:

```css
&[data-scrollable] {
  max-height: 240px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  scrollbar-width: none;
  -ms-overflow-style: none;
  &::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
}
```

Every scrollbar affordance suppressed on all three engines, with a 240px cap. So output is silently clipped with no cue that more exists or that it scrolls.

**D19 — content shift on session switch.** Recorded against your standing requirement. The fold decision depends on `settled`/`interrupted`/`foldableCount`, all derived from data arriving *after* mount — so the first frame paints one answer and re-folds when data lands. And `renderOverscan` starting at 1 for uncached sessions means a switch deliberately mounts degraded, then upgrades. With D12 and D20 that's three independent post-paint reflow sources on a single switch. The title loader flicker I did not trace.

**D22 — the aborted/failed card.** I couldn't narrow this one honestly. The `tool-error-card` CSS is actually restrained on its own, so it's probably not the offender. Worth knowing: `session-turn.tsx:292-299` routes `MessageAbortedError` to *interrupted* and any other error to the error card — so a user abort and a real failure land on different surfaces, and restyling the wrong one is easy. A screenshot or the exact card text would settle it in one pass.

Still outstanding and untouched: **D8** (subagent card width overflow).

